## Accountabilities

| Capability | Accountable owner | Responsibilities |
|---|---|---|
| Platform engineering | {{FACTORY-RAW:operations.platformTeam.name}} | Landing-zone code, shared services, upgrades, platform incidents |
| Application teams | Workload owners | Workload resources, application SLOs, remediation within delegated scopes |
| Security | Security operations | Policy exceptions, threat response, privileged-access review |
| Finance | {{FACTORY-RAW:finops.businessOwner.name}} | Budget ownership, allocation disputes, optimization decisions |
| Change approval | Configured approval chain | Production/environment approvals and emergency change review |

## Repository decision rights

- `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}` is the authoritative desired state.
- Pull requests are the only normal change path.
- Required approvals: {{FACTORY-NUM:github.branchProtection.requiredApprovals}}.
- Code-owner review required:
  {{FACTORY-BOOL:github.branchProtection.requireCodeOwnerReview}}.
- Stale approvals dismissed:
  {{FACTORY-BOOL:github.branchProtection.dismissStaleReviews}}.
- Administrators enforced:
  {{FACTORY-BOOL:github.branchProtection.enforceAdmins}}.
- Apply jobs bind to protected GitHub environments and use a distinct write
  identity. Pull requests use read-only plan identities.

## Service boundaries

The platform team owns these generated layers:

#{{FOREACH layer IN computed.layers}}
- `terraform/live/{{FACTORY-RAW:layer}}`
#{{ENDFOREACH}}

Each layer has isolated state and is planned/applied independently. Application
teams must not bypass module interfaces or edit state directly.

## Operating cadence

| Frequency | Activity | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Every pull request | Format, validate, policy, security, and plan checks | GitHub check run |
| Every approved apply | Layer-by-layer apply and post-apply verification | Workflow run and state version |
#{{IF defined observability.driftDetection.schedule}}
| Weekly | Drift detection (`{{FACTORY-RAW:observability.driftDetection.schedule}}`) | Drift issue or clean run |
#{{ELSE}}
| Weekly | Drift detection (no schedule configured — set `observability.driftDetection.schedule`) | Drift issue or clean run |
#{{ENDIF}}
| Monthly | Cost, privileged access, policy compliance, backup health | Review record |
| Quarterly | Restore exercise, break-glass test, architecture review | Exercise report |
| Annually | Threat model and disaster-recovery plan review | Signed review |

## Incident and escalation model

1. Stabilize the affected layer; do not make concurrent state changes.
2. Preserve workflow, activity-log, and Terraform evidence.
3. Notify {{FACTORY-RAW:operations.platformTeam.name}} and the accountable
   workload/security owner.
4. Use break-glass access only when normal federated access cannot restore
   service.
5. Reconcile emergency changes back through a pull request before closure.

Contacts and approval chains are sourced from `lz-config.json`. Empty contact
lists are an onboarding blocker that operators must resolve before production.

